WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:19.074
Danny: Whoo boy! This is going to be good.

2
00:00:19.075 --> 00:00:23.875
Brad: I just have to connect this wire to the battery . . .

3
00:00:23.876 --> 00:00:25.581
There, that's it.

4
00:00:25.582 --> 00:00:27.712
Danny: Will it work?

5
00:00:27.713 --> 00:00:32.922
Brad: Yes, if, as I expect, the nano-putty causes things to shrink.

6
00:00:32.923 --> 00:00:38.130
Danny: It says so on the box!

7
00:00:38.131 --> 00:00:40.919
Brad: Well, I guess it should work then.

8
00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:52.281
Danny: Let's try it!

9
00:00:52.282 --> 00:00:55.186
Danny: What about Tabby over there?

10
00:00:55.187 --> 00:00:58.796
Brad: No! What if . . . what if something went wrong?

11
00:00:58.797 --> 00:01:00.807
Danny: Nothing will go wrong.

12
00:01:00.808 --> 00:01:02.932
You said it would work.

13
00:01:02.933 --> 00:01:13.135
Brad: Well, yes. Nothing should go wrong . . .

14
00:01:13.136 --> 00:01:17.217
Brad: Let's test it on something that isn't alive.

15
00:01:17.218 --> 00:01:20.454
Danny: Fine.

16
00:01:20.455 --> 00:01:25.251
Brad: What about . . . that umbrella?

17
00:01:25.252 --> 00:01:34.666
Danny: That's boring. But sure, go ahead.

18
00:01:34.667 --> 00:01:37.197
Brad: Something happened!

19
00:01:37.198 --> 00:01:41.208
Danny: I still can't see . . .

20
00:01:41.209 --> 00:01:46.845
Brad: It's . . . I think I see . . . oh my!

21
00:01:46.846 --> 00:01:52.047
Danny: Wow!

22
00:01:52.048 --> 00:01:53.952
Danny: What went wrong?

23
00:01:53.953 --> 00:01:55.374
Brad: I don't know.

24
00:01:55.375 --> 00:01:59.692
Ah! The nano-streams must be crossed.

25
00:01:59.693 --> 00:02:02.342
Danny: So, instead of shrinking it . . .

26
00:02:02.343 --> 00:02:08.435
Brad: It made it bigger.

27
00:02:08.436 --> 00:02:10.935
Brad: What should we try it on next?

28
00:02:10.936 --> 00:02:16.386
Danny: I still think the cat is a good idea.

29
00:02:16.387 --> 00:02:18.261
Brad: How about that plant?

30
00:02:18.262 --> 00:02:21.904
It's a living thing, but it's not my pet.

31
00:02:21.905 --> 00:02:28.261
Danny: Let me do it this time!

32
00:02:28.262 --> 00:02:30.066
Brad: That was better.

33
00:02:30.067 --> 00:02:35.601
Danny: There was less smoke this time.

34
00:02:35.602 --> 00:02:38.573
Brad: It's got polka dots.

35
00:02:38.574 --> 00:02:42.566
Danny: It's not smaller at all.

36
00:02:42.567 --> 00:02:45.678
Danny: I don't think this nano-putty works!

37
00:02:45.679 --> 00:02:49.104
Brad: If my dad invented it, it works.

38
00:02:49.105 --> 00:02:52.206
Maybe I'm not doing something right.

39
00:02:52.207 --> 00:02:58.597
Danny: Still, it would be funny if the bullies were covered in polka dots.

40
00:02:58.598 --> 00:03:04.230
Danny: Hee-hee! They'd try to wash the dots off, but they wouldn't come off!

41
00:03:04.231 --> 00:03:06.127
Brad: Oops!

42
00:03:06.128 --> 00:03:07.429
Danny: What?

43
00:03:07.430 --> 00:03:14.922
Brad: I think this accidentally got in to the gun.

44
00:03:14.923 --> 00:03:17.059
Danny: How did that get in there?

45
00:03:17.060 --> 00:03:19.369
Brad: I don't know.

46
00:03:19.370 --> 00:03:24.265
Danny: You use pink polka-dotted Band-Aids? Ha-ha!

47
00:03:24.266 --> 00:03:26.114
Brad: I cut my finger.

48
00:03:26.115 --> 00:03:29.277
It was the only one I could find.

49
00:03:29.278 --> 00:03:33.519
Danny: Ha-ha! That's a Band-Aid for a baby girl!

50
00:03:33.520 --> 00:03:35.090
Brad: Don't laugh.

51
00:03:35.091 --> 00:03:38.528
Danny: Oooh. Did your mommy kiss it better?

52
00:03:38.529 --> 00:03:50.215
Brad: Stop teasing! No wonder the bullies don't like you.
